# shellcheck shell=sh
# Owner-only files for nish's login shells, which is how the Devin CLI and tmux
# start on this box. pam_umask sets a session to 0002 (UMASK 022 in
# /etc/login.defs with USERGROUPS_ENAB yes), so the CLI's run logs under
# ~/.local/share/devin came out group-writable (audit W1a,
# Nishfleet/nish-vault#30). systemd-started launchers carry their own
# UMask=0077; this file covers the shell ones. zsh reads it for login shells
# only: sshd starts nish's shell as a login shell, and a tmux server started
# from it hands the umask to its panes. nish is the only zsh user (root runs
# bash). sudo takes the union of the invoking umask with 0022, so a root
# command run from such a shell also writes 0600 files: anything a service must
# read needs its mode set, which the playbook does for every file it installs.
umask 077
